{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And every man's holy things shall be his</b> – The correct interpretation of this verse is that it states that all of a person's holy things shall be his, meaning that all sacred donations regarding which he is not commanded to give them to the priest shall belong to the owners, and they are permitted to use them even though they are called holy. And <b>the man who gives to the priest, it shall be to him</b> — even the holy things that the verse commands to give to the priest, the owners retain a right in them, for they belong to that particular priest to whom the man gives them, as his property. Now, second tithe and fourth-year planting, concerning which the verse says they shall be holy to YHWH (Leviticus 27:30, ibid. 19:24), belong to the man as his property, and likewise the tithe of animals (ibid. 27:32). But the rest of the holy things concerning which he commands in the portion of \"And Korach took\" (Numbers 18), which they are to give to the priest — they are given to him from the hand of the owners, not that the priests may seize them from them by force. And from our verse we learn that the right of enjoyment (tovat hana'ah) belongs to the owners. This is the straightforward meaning, and it is the opinion of Onkelos (Onkelos on Numbers 5:10). And in this manner it is expounded in the Sifrei (Sifrei Naso 31), they said: All sacred donations were included in what is stated, <b>\"And every man's holy things shall be his\"</b>, etc. The verse drew all sacred donations and gave them to the priests, and did not exclude from them anything except the thanksgiving offering, the peace offerings, the Paschal offering, the tithe of animals, the second tithe, and the fourth-year planting, which belong to the owners. They mentioned also the thanksgiving offering, the peace offerings, and the Paschal offering because they too belong to the owners, but this verse was not needed for them at all."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:02:59.109485873Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}